## Appendix Q: Reporting Standards and Claim Certainty Grades

All findings must be reported with explicit certainty grades:

- **Definitive** (≥95% posterior probability, robust to unmeasured confounding E-value >2.0): Rare, requires high-quality evidence across multiple phases.
- **Robust** (80–95% posterior probability, E-value >1.5, survives red-team review): Most published claims should reach this level.
- **Plausible** (60–80% posterior probability, E-value >1.2): Interesting but preliminary; recommend replication.
- **Speculative** (<60% posterior probability, E-value <1.2, or validation failed): Hypothesis-generating; not suitable for high-stakes decisions without further evidence.

**Example Report**:
> "Claim: Images rank higher than text posts on average.
> - Posterior P(images > text): 82%
> - Effect size (median): 0.25 SD [95% CI: 0.0–0.6]
> - E-value: 1.85 (robust to unmeasured confounders with RR ≤ 1.85)
